  "question_stem": "A particle $P$ travels in a straight line, starting at rest from a point $O$. The acceleration of $P$ at time $t\\text{ s}$ after leaving $O$ is denoted by $a\\text{ m s}^{-2}$, where\n$$\\begin{aligned} a &= 0.3t^{\\frac{1}{2}} &&\\text{for } 0 \\le t \\le 4, \\\\ a &= -kt^{-\\frac{3}{2}} &&\\text{for } 4 < t \\le T, \\end{aligned}$$\nwhere $k$ and $T$ are constants.",
  "context_texts": [
    "$1.6\\,\\mathrm{m\\,s^{-1}}$",
    "$k=2.6$ and $v=5.2t^{-1/2}-1$",
    "$T=\\frac{676}{25}$ (i.e. $27.04$)."
  ],
